 tom on May 04, 2019:↵↵Very weird because this is not my first time like this. Keep up the great hub.↵↵iammezio (author) from colona, doc on February 12, 2018:↵↵Err, Topical Note: Strains of cyanobacteria are able to kill molds if brought inside.↵↵CheysburgDerrick from Eugene, Oregon on February 01, 2013:↵↵thanks, Annette!↵↵My most bizarre mold encounter was when I was 7 years old plus. My brother and I were on the beach out by Monterey Bay, huge kelp trees just came up. (We went several times a year there.) The air was foggy, very cold, so I bent down to look at the glassy water but it was pretty briny. Okay, thinking, I may have seen some gnarly moths on the surface, but I didn't think there was anything bad.↵↵Went up vertically and saw a fairly large, very boxy looking moth. I thought the plate-like thing was just some sort of weed. I couldn't believe it and started patty crawling around in the jacuzzi for moulds
